The `normalise` helper creates a `PrecompiledCharMapNormalizer` (which extends `Reader`) but never closes it. Since this is called in a loop over multiple inputs in `testOutOfBounds`, consider wrapping it in a try-with-resources block to avoid leaking the underlying `StringReader` and any internal buffers:
```java
try (PrecompiledCharMapNormalizer normalizer = new PrecompiledCharMapNormalizer(...)) {
    // read loop
}
```
